| Technique  | Purpose                           |
| ---------- | --------------------------------- |
| Lag        | Previous values (t-1, t-2)        |
| Difference | Remove trend                      |
| Log        | Reduce variance and smooth growth |


==============

| Lag                                   | Difference                                    | Log                                                      |    |
| ------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- | -- |
| Previous observation (t-1, t-2, etc.) | Current value minus previous value            | Mathematical transformation of the value                 |    |
| Used for forecasting features         | Used to remove trend and achieve stationarity | Used to stabilize variance and handle exponential growth |    |
| Example: 180                          | Example: 220−180=40                           | Example: log(220)=2.34                                   |    |

=============

| Technique  | Analogy                                             |
| ---------- | --------------------------------------------------- |
| Lag        | Looking at yesterday's sales                        |
| Difference | Checking how much sales changed from yesterday      |
| Log        | Compressing very large numbers into smaller numbers |


